            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en" resp="#AA">
                <p>
                    To Numisia Secunda Sabina, [wife of] Claudius Liber, sacerdos of the Augusta, m[other?] of the municipium and colonia of Interamna Praetuttiorum,
                    on account of her munificence. To this woman, the first of all, the Pratuttian populace of women set up [this] statue with collected money; on 
                    the dedication of which, she gave to each citizen four sesterces. This place [was given by] decree [of the decurions].
                </p>
